nfidence":0.96},{"symptom":"fever, during","chapter":"nose","parent":"EPISTAXIS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"c97faa587a24691a837894b7","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"intensely red before the attack","chapter":"nose","parent":"EPISTAXIS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"9beaf5c055969e25e4058564","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"FULNESS","chapter":"rectum","parent":"Aloe, ant-c. , cain., carb-an., carb-v.,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"d7250d343253122d35f41175","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"COPIOUS (increased)","chapter":"urine","parent":"CONSTITUENTS, where there is diminution of,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"279ea41ac67d2526d13f1139","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"which amel","chapter":"urine","parent":"COPIOUS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"95f1f71d5ac0e6da9642bba6","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"MOVING the head","chapter":"vertigo","parent":"MENTAL","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"abbf49252f0ae1c7403742f7","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.8},{"symptom":"STOOPING, on","chapter":"vertigo","parent":null,"evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"93aeb5b5f2c4885283553b59","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.8},{"symptom":"during","chapter":"vision","parent":"COLORS, black","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"8d010d024edc11eb56b4a541","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96}],"sections":[{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"mind","label":"Mind","startLine":22273,"endLine":22277,"text":"Unable to fix mind. Memory treacherous.\nStupor. Wants to run away and hide. Delusions;\nthinks every one is looking at her, fears to talk loud,\nand wants to run away, etc."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"head","label":"Head","startLine":22278,"endLine":22282,"text":"Headache with retching, vomiting, sense of\npres.sure over orbits, pallor, cold hands and feet, black\nspots before eyes. Heavy, oppressed; frontal, throb-\nbing, undulating sensation in brain. Sick headache ; re-\nlieved by epistaxis or menstrual flow. Fullness all over"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"head","label":"head","startLine":22283,"endLine":22286,"text":"Eyes heavy; blurred sight; wants to close them\ntightly for relief. Neuralgia around and over right side\nof head and neck. Scalp sore* and tender to touch."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"nose","label":"Nose","startLine":22287,"endLine":22289,"text":"Stopped up, dry, must breathe through\nmouth ; dry, hard clinkers in nose ; profuse epistaxis."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"face","label":"Face","startLine":22290,"endLine":22292,"text":"Intensely red and flushed, with throbbing\ncarotids, [Bell.]"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"stool","label":"Stool","startLine":22293,"endLine":22296,"text":"Difficult, painful, constipated. Anus feels\nconstricted, full, throbs. No desire until there is a large\naccumulation. [Bry.; Alum.]"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"female","label":"Female","startLine":22297,"endLine":22300,"text":"Menses scanty, intermit, with nausea and\nbearing-down. Sticking pain in external parts. Dys-\nmenorrhoca. Ovarian neuralgia."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"respiratory","label":"Respiratory","startLine":22301,"endLine":22304,"text":"Feels as if smothering, especially from\nrapid walking. Haemoptysis. Weight on chest. Tick-\nling in throat with cough."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"extremities","label":"Extremities","startLine":22305,"endLine":22308,"text":"Pain in knee ; wants to stretch leg, but\ndoes not relieve. Joints sore. Skin and extremities\ncold. Numbness and aching in knee-joints."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"modalities","label":"Modalities","startLine":22309,"endLine":22311,"text":"Worse, rainy, changeable weather, ap-\nproach of storm, motion; 4 p. m."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"relationship","label":"Relationship","startLine":22312,"endLine":22316,"text":"Compare: Melilotus alba (White\nClover — practically the same action. (Haemorrhages,\ncongestive headaches, engorged blood vessels, spasms.)\nAmyl' Bell.; Glon."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"head","label":"Head","startLine":38360,"endLine":38364,"text":"Frequent headache, with but little pain,®.—At 9 p.m., after a\nhard day’s work accomplished by an effort, I had a horrible opi)ressive\nheadache, felt dizzy, faint, and nauseated (second day),®.—The odor gave\nsome of the people a terribly oppressive headache,'®."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"face","label":"Face","startLine":38365,"endLine":38368,"text":"Very red face in the afternoon (second day),®.\n\nSfonifteh ,—Acrid and burning eructations all the evening (first day),®."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"abdomen","label":"Abdomen","startLine":38369,"endLine":38375,"text":"Before I got to sleep, my abdomen became considerably\nbloated, with a crawling sensation as of worms, near the rectal muscles\n(second night),®.\n\nIll’inart/ Orf/ans. —Was obliged to void water very frequently\n(fourth day),®."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"chest","label":"Chest","startLine":38376,"endLine":38401,"text":"Before 10 p.m., had a severe pain apparently in right lung,\nwith occasionally a pain in left hip, with twitching or jactitation of the\nmuscles (second day),®.—[40.] Awoke after sle^)ing badly, with a great\ndeal of soreness in my chest internally, with an oppression as of a great\nweight. Through the day I had much difficulty in breathing, and every\nrespiration was labored, with a continued fulness of the chest and head\n(third day). Awoke with a spasmodic cough, and yet with the same op¬\npression and spasmodic breathing and fulness of the chest. Repeatedly\nexamined my clothing to see if it did not oppress me; feared that I had\ntaken cold and would have pneumonia. Was extremely nervous, and\nduring the day the severe, oppressive, heavy, and throbbing headache re¬\nturned, so much so, I feared some of the bloodvessels would give way and\nsome lesion of the brain would occur. Was easiest when perfectly quiet.\nTowards night was sure I had internal haemorrhage from the severe con¬\ngestion and fulness (fourth day). Had a horribly distressing cough, which\ngave me a great deal of anxiety. Very easily wearied, with inability to\nget air enough ; the head was better. Towards night a slight expectora¬\ntion took place, which gave me some little relief, but it was detached with\ngreat difficulty. Was obliged to give up business, go home, and all night\nhad hot cloths ap])lied to my chest to give relief. Was delirious part of\nthe night, and talked almost constantly (fifth day). The next day was\nunable to attend to my business, but, finally recovered in a few days,®.\n\nGeneralities. —Felt oppressed, heavy, and tired, in the morning\n{second day),®."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"sleep","label":"Sleep","startLine":38402,"endLine":38402,"text":"Felt sleepy and dull, in the afternoon (second day),®."},{"source":"12_boger_synoptic_key","section":"head","label":"HEAD","startLine":31525,"endLine":31599,"text":"Vaso-motor nerves.\nCirculation.\n\nWORSE:\n\nClimacteric.\n\nWalking.\n\nWeather: Changing. Stormy. Rainy.\n\nBETTER:\nBleeding.\nProfuse urine.\nVinegar.\n\nRaw feeling. Congestions. Bright red heemorrhage; which >. ................0.. Desires to escape.\nRushes of blood to head. VIOLENT, THROBBING HEADACHE; threatens his reason; >\nnosebleed. FIERY RED FACE. Profuse nosebleed. Dry skin.\n\nRelated: Bell. Glo.\n\nMENYANTHES TRIFOLIATA\n\nREGION:\nCirculation.\nMotor nerves.\nVertex.\n\nWORSE:\nWalking.\nRest.\nMalaria.\nAscending.\nQuinine.\n\nBETTER:\n\nHard pressure.\nTwilight.\n\nLaying on hands.\n\nIcy coldness of prominent, single or affected parts; nose (Ap. Med.), ears, fingers, knees,\nabdomen, etc.; at night (Pho.). Visible jerks or twitches. Vertex; heavy pressure on; pains, <\nstooping; or as of a weight in nape. Bursting headache. Pain ascends from nape. Misty vision.\nFrequent, scant urine. Boring at |. scapula. Cramp in posterior thighs, < sitting, or from ankles to\ncalves (r). Skin feels tight. Vivid dreams. Shivering, with yawning. Quartan malaria.\n\nRelated: Ver-a.\n\nMEPHITIS PUTORIUS\n\nREGION:\nNerves.\n\nWORSE:\nLying.\n\nNight.\n\nAfter menses.\n\nBETTER:\nCold bath or weather.\n\nSpasmodic effects. Foul breath and expectoration. Debility after severe illness. Trembling and\ntwitching of exophthalmos. ..............06 Excitable. Loquacious. Vivid fancies. Violent vertigo.\nAs of a finger pressing on occiput. Food goes the wrong way. Chokes easily. Can't exhale.\nAsthma. Asthma of consumptives or drunkards. Cough; violent; spasmodic; nervous;\nsuffocative; whooping; < talking or drinking. Choking cough.\n\nRelated: Coral. Mosch."}],"corpusPassages":[]}